      "role": "user",
      "content": "hey im seeing a CrashLoopBackOff on my auth-service pod in gke. logs show:\n`Error: Cannot find module '/app/dist/index.js' thrown by process`\nand then it just exits. i already checked the dockerfile and the entrypoint looks right. can u give me a checklist of what to look at to figure out if its a config issue or something else?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a checklist to troubleshoot your crash loop: Verify that the `NODE_ENV` environment variable matches what your build script expects, as mismatches can cause lazy compilation errors. Ensure your Dockerfile's build arguments correctly resolve to runtime environment variables if they are required for the build step. Finally, confirm that GKE is injecting the expected env vars by using `kubectl exec` to list them inside the pod and double-checking the `特权` (privileged) or `container privileges` if applicable.\n\nAfter verifying your logs again with `--all-containers=true` and `--tail=100`, specifically look for any build-time warnings that might resolve to runtime failures.",
